{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And in their carcasses you shall not touch.</b> If they died of their own death, you shall not touch them in order to eat them — as we say regarding ״בכל קדש לא תגע״ in tractate Makkot, that it is a warning against eating, and the Merciful One expressed it in the language of touching, in order to set the measure for one who touches as for one who eats. Here too the Merciful One expressed eating in the language of touching, and the doubled phrase — לא תאכלו ולא תגעו — is one matter. For if it means literal touching, why is eating written? If He warned about touching, eating is all the more so. Nevertheless, our Rabbis said that it speaks of literal touching, and it is a warning for Israel on the festival, as the Master said: a person is obligated to purify himself on the festival."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:56.716530224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}